{"seq":1207,"lane":"drop","class":"fiscal-year-drop","severity":"serious","evidence":"1207.json: A proposed “What year-over-year total revenue growth will NVIDIA report for FY2028?”; handover dropped it as “year 2028 is beyond next year”.","rule":"Standard §3–4: a company's annual quantity uses its fiscal year and may cover the current or next fiscal year.","mechanism":"Record preparation returned bare “2028”, so the run's year check treated the fiscal year as a calendar year. split-v2-design.md §6 says this was corrected after the confirmation run."}
{"seq":1207,"lane":"B","class":"unhelpful-revenue-link","severity":"serious","evidence":"1207.json: “CME Group plans to launch futures on Oct. 5 tied to the hourly rental cost of Nvidia's H100 and B200 graphics processors, pending regulatory approval” was linked to v2, “What will NVIDIA report as total revenue for FY2027?”","rule":"Standard §5.1 and §5.3: evidence must make an answer more or less likely; D273 and D361 retain the revenue fallback for evidence bearing on demand, supply, competition or pricing.","mechanism":"B appears to use the company-wide revenue fallback for an announcement about a proposed trading instrument without identifying how it changes NVIDIA's revenue."}
{"seq":1208,"lane":"matching","class":"invented-statement-date","severity":"serious","evidence":"1208.json: “Also announced recently is a $12.9 billion acquisition of AI specialist Hugging Face” has original_day “”; matching returned “replace” and said_day “2026-08-29”.","rule":"D203: an unknown original statement day stays unknown; D202 requires a later account for a revision.","mechanism":"src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:265 substitutes the article publication day when original_day is empty, exposing the replacement decision to an unsupported date."}
{"seq":1209,"lane":"record_preparation","class":"unusable-question","severity":"serious","evidence":"1209.json: v70 asks “How much has NVIDIA committed to memory and advanced-packaging supply through 2032, as disclosed by its FY2027 annual report?”; it was written with due_day “”, rungs [] and judgements [].","rule":"Standard §3 and §4: an assumed obligation is an amount question with five outcomes and a check at the next annual report; a question must be verifiable at a date.","mechanism":"The preparation request allows an empty date and an empty ladder when it finds no reference; build_handover accepts both and writes the question. The trace does not establish that a precise ladder could be derived from this article."}
{"seq":1210,"lane":"B","class":"quote-summary-mismatch","severity":"serious","evidence":"1210.json handover e1 quotes “During second-quarter earnings, Nvidia CFO Colette Kress revealed that the company will be spending $279 billion on supply commitments over the next few years -- up from $119 billion only three months earlier. The reason for the jump is primarily about memory.” Its one_line additionally says “with $92 billion due in the rest of FY2027 and $87 billion and $88 billion in FY2028 and FY2029, respectively”.","rule":"Standard §2 requires a verbatim passage and a standalone summary of the recorded statement, with accurate attribution.","mechanism":"B combined separated passages into one quote; source_quote retained the intact opening passage, while build_handover kept the longer summary unchanged. The additional amounts occur elsewhere in the article, but not in the retained quote."}
{"seq":1211,"lane":"B","class":"wrong-evidence-home","severity":"serious","evidence":"1211.json: “Within the data center book, hyperscale customers contributed $48.7 billion of revenue -- an increase of 102% year over year” was linked to v2, the total-revenue question, rather than v10, the Data Center revenue question.","rule":"D207 and standard §5–6: file helpful evidence under the narrowest open question it bears on.","mechanism":"B selected the broad company-revenue question even though the passage expressly identifies the narrower segment."}
{"seq":1211,"lane":"B","class":"wrong-evidence-home","severity":"serious","evidence":"1211.json: “Operating income rose 19% sequentially and 124% year over year to $63.7 billion” was linked to v13, “What profit will NVIDIA report for FY2027?”, but not v25, “What operating margin will NVIDIA report for FY2027?”","rule":"Standard §5.1 and D259: retain figures that help answer an existing question; D207 calls for the narrowest applicable question.","mechanism":"B did not connect operating income to the operating-margin question, even though the same article supplies total revenue needed to interpret the figure."}
{"seq":1211,"lane":"record_preparation","class":"unusable-question","severity":"serious","evidence":"1211.json: v71 asks “What gross margin will NVIDIA report for FY2028?” and was written with due_day “”, rungs [] and judgements []; the source says margin is expected to bottom “between 71% and 72% by the fourth quarter before recovering in fiscal 2028”.","rule":"Standard §3–4 requires five outcomes and a date for an annual quantity. The preparation request permits a recent or part-year figure as a stated comparison.","mechanism":"Record preparation left the ladder empty despite receiving the prior-quarter margin and the near-term margin outlook; the handover accepts an empty ladder and date."}
{"seq":1227,"lane":"record_preparation","class":"unusable-question","severity":"serious","evidence":"1227.json: v73 asks “How much capital expenditure will Alphabet report for fiscal 2026?” and has five rungs and daily judgements, but due_day is “”.","rule":"Standard §3–4: an annual quantity has a check date tied to publication of the result; its outcome must be verifiable at a date.","mechanism":"META_SYSTEM requires an exact date in the source or A's check description and otherwise leaves it empty; A names the annual report but no exact day, and build_handover accepts the empty date."}
{"seq":1227,"lane":"record_preparation","class":"rung-boundary-mismatch","severity":"serious","evidence":"1227.json v73: the neutral condition says “at most 215250000000 USD”, while its numeric hi is 215250000000; the next condition says “above 215250000000 USD” while its lo is 215250000000.","rule":"Standard §3 requires mutually exclusive outcomes with no gaps; META_SYSTEM defines numeric lower bounds as inclusive and upper bounds as exclusive.","mechanism":"check_bounds checks that adjacent numeric bounds meet but does not check whether the written conditions agree with those bounds. At exactly $215.25 billion, the text and numeric fields identify different outcomes."}
{"seq":1228,"lane":"record_preparation","class":"currency-basis-ambiguity","severity":"minor","evidence":"1228.json: v74 asks for “revenue growth” Microsoft will report for FY2027, while its neutral comparison is “45% constant-currency Azure growth guidance for fiscal Q1 2027”; the judgement says the evidence does not quantify an adjustment to the eventual reported full-year figure.","rule":"Standard §4 requires a question's measurement scope to be clear and its outcome verifiable; §3 requires the middle outcome to state its comparison.","mechanism":"Record preparation carried a constant-currency quarterly reference into a question that does not specify the currency basis of the annual result."}
{"summary":{"items_read":2,"items_fully_reviewed":[1205,1206],"items_incompletely_reviewed":[1207,1208,1209,1210,1211,1212,1213,1214,1215,1216,1217,1218,1219,1220,1221,1222,1223,1224,1225,1226,1227,1228,1229,1230],"classes":{"fiscal-year-drop":1,"unhelpful-revenue-link":1,"invented-statement-date":1,"unusable-question":3,"quote-summary-mismatch":1,"wrong-evidence-home":2,"rung-boundary-mismatch":1,"currency-basis-ambiguity":1}}}

